## Limits and operational notes

The authenticated three-universe V5 bundle remains unavailable. No real manifest/panel artifact emission, market evaluation, later-stage eligibility, qualification opening, or replay was attempted. Fixture evidence is explicitly synthetic; it proves controller mechanics and feedback persistence, not policy performance.

Windows Python temporary-directory ACL behavior rejected two initially created empty directories, and deeply nested scratch paths exceeded the platform's practical path limit. Subsequent direct checks used short, shell-created worktree-local scratch paths. These were verification-environment limitations; no production filesystem/authentication guard was weakened. The detailed direct script is uncommitted campaign working material, and the focused commit contains source changes only.

Cleanup confirmation: all synthetic scratch repositories were removed after exact worktree-boundary checks. The two empty ACL-restricted directory attempts were removed through narrowly scoped, automatically approved elevation. Final read-only enumeration reported zero synthetic scratch directories remaining. No user data or real campaign artifacts were removed.
